// Offset of the RAMDRIVE volume-label entry within the blob.
// On 3a v3.40f the kernel writes its label at ram[0x86660], so
// overlaying the blob at base = 0x86660 - 0x4200 = 0x82460
// reproduces the 3c byte layout. Siena writes its label at
// ram[0x7dff0]; the 3c blob does not fit (32 KiB ≥ Siena top RAM)
// and the v4.20f kernel uses a smaller, top-anchored layout, so
// Siena needs a separate (smaller) blob to be captured from a
// known-good Siena boot.
static constexpr uint32_t kMDriveBlobLabelOffset = 0x4200;

